# =============================================================================
# .pip-audit-ignore — Temporary pip-audit suppressions
# =============================================================================
#
# Read by .github/workflows/security.yml, which converts each non-comment,
# non-blank line into a `--ignore-vuln <ID>` flag passed to pip-audit.
# pip-audit has no native ignore-file format; this is the project-local
# convention.
#
# Rules (mirrors .trivyignore):
#   1. Every entry MUST have an expiration date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
#   2. Every entry MUST link to an upstream tracking issue/advisory.
#   3. When an entry expires, re-evaluate: remove it if the CVE is fixed,
#      or extend the date with a new justification if the fix still isn't
#      available. Never extend without re-checking upstream.
#   4. Keep the file short. A growing ignorefile is a smell.
#
# Format (whitespace flexible, anything after `#` is a comment):
#   <PYSEC-or-GHSA-or-CVE-ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# =============================================================================

